{
  "rationale": "The binding constraint is the system burst: a 1 MHz tick dumps 32 requests that must ALL be back within 0.44 us. That is ~73 MSPS sustained during the burst, and it is a hard structural filter. Only families that emit one result per cycle can pipeline a 32-deep burst: pipelined (1/cyc, N+2 latency) and pipelined_m (1/cyc, ceil(N/m)+2 latency). iterative (1 result per N+3 cycles) and unrolled_k (1 per ceil(N/k)+3 cycles) would need 32*(N+3) or 32*(ceil(N/k)+3) cycles for a burst — at any plausible Fmax that is >0.44 us, so they should fail the L1 batch bound and are only worth a small confirmation share. Accuracy (max_abs_err <= 2^-12, i.e. accuracy_bits >= 12) needs roughly N>=13 and W>=15 (output LSB = 2^-(W-2)), so the interesting accuracy range is N~13..20, W~14..20. The objective is min luts_plus_ffs, and pipelined_m is the area lever: registering every m stages cuts the pipeline register count from N to ceil(N/m)+2 at the cost of Fmax, which is exactly the trade-off the front should map. Round 1 therefore concentrates on pipelined_m and pipelined over the accuracy-feasible region, with a small probe of unrolled_k/iterative to document infeasibility. Later rounds will tighten around the feasible front and push m, N, W to their extremes.",
