{
  "rationale": "Round 2 front is entirely pipelined_m and already covers both objective ranges well: luts_plus_ffs 1211..3593 against HV ref 4000, and accuracy_bits 12.4..23.5 against HV ref 12. So the front is NOT confined to a small part of either range, and map_front is not yet the right call. The other families are dead ends for this spec: iterative (10 evals, 0 feasible, max throughput 15.6 MSPS) and unrolled_k (15 evals, 0 feasible, max 12 MSPS) both miss the >=32 MSPS constraint, and pipelined is dominated by pipelined_m (best feasible luts_plus_ffs 1970 vs 1211). The selection rule is min luts_plus_ffs, and the cheapest feasible point is 1211 (data_width=19, n_iter=14, m=3), with the next points at 1337/1609/1922 - i.e. the low-area end is where both the selection rule and most of the HV area live, and where the accuracy constraint (2^-12) is tightest (12.4 bits at W=19). Refining pipelined_m around that cheap/mid region should either find sub-1211 feasible designs or densify the steep part of the curve, while the high-accuracy tail (W=28, 23.5 bits) is already mapped. Gain is still +132%, so not a stop.",
